# Replacements for the per-expression profiler

*plugin* `profiler`

All worker-only hooks call `self.dsm_profiler?.…`. The shared module is also
evaluated on the main thread, where `dsm_profiler` is not defined, so the hooks
are no-ops there. In the worker, every hook is a cheap no-op unless recording.

## Time analysis of each statement

*Description* `Profile analysis (compile) time per statement`

*worker_only*

*Find* => `from`
```js
let $l = this.analyzeSingleStatement($u, $o, $n, $i, $s), $p = [];
```

*Replace* `from` with
```js
self.dsm_profiler?.beginAnalysis($u, $s);
let $l = this.analyzeSingleStatement($u, $o, $n, $i, $s);
self.dsm_profiler?.endAnalysis($u, $l);
let $p = [];
```

## Time compiling click handlers and domains of each statement

*Description* `Profile compile time after the main analysis (click handlers, domains) per statement`

*worker_only*

After analyzing every statement, Desmos compiles click handlers and
parametric domains in a separate loop. Count that as the statement's compile.

*Find* => `from`
```js
$k.graphingEnabled() && $XY(this.analysis[$id], this.moduleContexts.getPolicyContext(this.assertFullStatement($id).moduleID), $Fx(this.mainFrameContext, $L), $k)
```

*Replace* `from` with
```js
$k.graphingEnabled() && (
  self.dsm_profiler?.beginPostAnalysis($id),
  $XY(this.analysis[$id], this.moduleContexts.getPolicyContext(this.assertFullStatement($id).moduleID), $Fx(this.mainFrameContext, $L), $k),
  self.dsm_profiler?.endPostAnalysis($id)
)
```

## Time parsing each statement

*Description* `Profile parse time per statement`

*worker_only*

*Find* => `from`
```js
this.addStatement($n, $hv($t.defaultModuleId))
```

*Replace* `from` with
```js
(
  self.dsm_profiler?.beginParse($n.id),
  this.addStatement($n, $hv($t.defaultModuleId)),
  self.dsm_profiler?.endParse($n.id)
)
```

## Time computing graph data of each statement

*Description* `Profile graph (sampling/meshing) time per statement`

*worker_only*

*Find* => `from`
```js
let $p = $cde(this.analysis, $s, $c, this.postProgressUpdate.bind(this), this.childIntersections), $m = [];
```

*Replace* `from` with
```js
self.dsm_profiler?.beginGraph($s);
let $p = $cde(this.analysis, $s, $c, this.postProgressUpdate.bind(this), this.childIntersections);
self.dsm_profiler?.endGraph($s);
let $m = [];
```

## Send the profile of each change set to the main thread

*Description* `Attach the per-expression profile to timingData`

*worker_only*

*Find* => `from`
```js
$o.timeInWorker = $a - $n;
```

*Replace* `from` with
```js
$o.timeInWorker = $a - $n,
$o.dsmProfile = self.dsm_profiler?.drainChangeSet();
```

## Attribute compile time to inlined global identifiers

Desmos compiles a reference to a global by inlining its definition at the use
site. This is what makes "wackscope" work (the definition is compiled in the
scope of the use), and it means the cost of a definition shows up in every
statement that uses it, so we record it per source symbol.

*Description* `Profile compile time of each inlined identifier`

*worker_only*

*Find* => `from`
```js
let $P;
if ($S instanceof $Cls) $P = $Ze($e, $S);
else {
  let $E = $o.newLexicalScope(), $M = $wa($e, $E);
  $P = $Ze($M, $S)
}
return $o.cacheGlobal($y, $P, $S), $P
```

*Replace* `from` with
```js
let $P;
const __dsmFrame = self.dsm_profiler?.enter($y, "id");
try {
  if ($S instanceof $Cls) $P = $Ze($e, $S);
  else {
    let $E = $o.newLexicalScope(), $M = $wa($e, $E);
    $P = $Ze($M, $S)
  }
} finally {
  self.dsm_profiler?.exit(__dsmFrame);
}
return $o.cacheGlobal($y, $P, $S), $P
```

## Count references resolved from an already-compiled identifier

*Description* `Profile cache hits of inlined identifiers`

*worker_only*

*Find* => `from`
```js
let $b = $o.getSymbol($y);
if ($b !== void 0) return $b;
```

*Replace* `from` with
```js
let $b = $o.getSymbol($y);
if ($b !== void 0) {
  self.dsm_profiler?.hit($y);
  return $b;
}
```

## Attribute compile time to inlined user function calls

*Description* `Profile compile time of each inlined function call`

*worker_only*

*Find* => `from`
```js
return $t.recursionInfo ? $G8($s, $t, $t.recursionInfo) : $Ze($s, $t._expression)
```

*Replace* `from` with
```js
const __dsmFrame = self.dsm_profiler?.enter($t._symbol, "fn");
try {
  return $t.recursionInfo ? $G8($s, $t, $t.recursionInfo) : $Ze($s, $t._expression)
} finally {
  self.dsm_profiler?.exit(__dsmFrame);
}
```

## Attribute compile time to pieces of expressions

Every parse node keeps the span of source LaTeX it came from, so timing each
node's compile breaks an expression down into its parts. Constant folding
happens here too, so for constant expressions this covers their evaluation.

*Description* `Profile compile time of each parse node`

*worker_only*

*Find* => `from`
```js
$n = $Cae($e, $t), $n = $Eae($e, $i, $n), $Iae($e, $n);
```

*Replace* `from` with
```js
{
  const __dsmNode = self.dsm_profiler?.enterNode($t);
  try {
    $n = $Cae($e, $t);
  } finally {
    self.dsm_profiler?.exit(__dsmNode);
  }
}
$n = $Eae($e, $i, $n), $Iae($e, $n);
```

## Tag 3D meshes with their expression id

*Description* `Tag 3D meshes with their expression id for profiling`

*worker_only*

*Find* => `from`
```js
finalizeSurface($t) {
```

*Replace* `from` with
```js
finalizeSurface($t) {
  self.dsm_profiler?.tagSurface($t);
```

## Track which expression each 3D draw call belongs to

*Description* `Track the expression of each 3D draw call`

*worker_only*

*Find* => `from`
```js
renderBufferDirect = function ($X, $ve, $Ge, $Tt, $Or, $cr) {
```

*Replace* `from` with
```js
renderBufferDirect = function ($X, $ve, $Ge, $Tt, $Or, $cr) {
  self.dsm_profiler?.setDrawObject($Or);
```

## Time three.js program setup (including shader compiles) per draw

*Description* `Profile 3D program setup per expression`

*worker_only*

*Find* => `from`
```js
$bn = $rj($X, $ve, $Tt, $Or);
$Ce.setMaterial($Tt, $En);
```

*Replace* `from` with
```js
$bn = self.dsm_profiler
  ? self.dsm_profiler.timeSetProgram(() => $rj($X, $ve, $Tt, $Or))
  : $rj($X, $ve, $Tt, $Or);
$Ce.setMaterial($Tt, $En);
```

## Send the profile of each 3D frame to the main thread

*Description* `Attach the per-expression profile to 3D render info`

*worker_only*

*Find* => `from`
```js
$M.durationCPU = performance.now() - $s,
```

*Replace* `from` with
```js
$M.durationCPU = performance.now() - $s,
$M.dsmProfile = self.dsm_profiler?.drainFrame(),
```

## Tell the worker whether to profile

*Description* `Send profiler flags with each worker message`

*Find* => `from`
```js
this.worker.postMessage({ connectionId: this.guid, originalMessage: $e }, $t)
```

*Replace* `from` with
```js
this.worker.postMessage({
  connectionId: this.guid,
  originalMessage: $e,
  dsmProfiler: window.DSM?.profiler?.workerFlags()
}, $t)
```

## Receive 3D frame profiles

*Description* `Receive per-expression 3D frame profiles`

*Find* => `from`
```js
case "redraw3dResult":
  this.onRedraw3dResults($t.payload);
```

*Replace* `from` with
```js
case "redraw3dResult":
  window.DSM?.profiler?.onRedraw3dResult($t.payload);
  this.onRedraw3dResults($t.payload);
```

## Time canvas drawing of each sketch

*Description* `Profile 2D canvas drawing per expression`

*Find* => `from`
```js
$r.drawSketchToCtx({
  sketch: $t[$u],
  drawContext: $e,
  poiLabelsLayer: $i,
  clickableObjectsLayer: $a,
  geometryContext: this.controller.getGeoModel()
})
```

*Replace* `from` with
```js
(window.DSM?.profiler
  ? window.DSM.profiler.timeSketch($t[$u], () => $r.drawSketchToCtx({
      sketch: $t[$u],
      drawContext: $e,
      poiLabelsLayer: $i,
      clickableObjectsLayer: $a,
      geometryContext: this.controller.getGeoModel()
    }))
  : $r.drawSketchToCtx({
      sketch: $t[$u],
      drawContext: $e,
      poiLabelsLayer: $i,
      clickableObjectsLayer: $a,
      geometryContext: this.controller.getGeoModel()
    }))
```
